# Deref-store missing-clone UAF regression (R2 SAFETY).
#
# `*box = borrowed_string` writes a value INTO an OWNED pointee (the
# Box[String] heap slot). The RHS `original` is a borrowed/live source —
# it is read again after the store (`original = original + " world"`).
#
# Pre-fix, the `Expr::Deref` arm of `lower_assign` lowered the RHS and
# called `emit_field_store_with_cleanup` DIRECTLY, WITHOUT routing through
# `clone_ptr_rhs_if_needed` (the discipline every other consuming position
# runs). So the borrowed `original` was shallow-copied into the owned
# pointee — both alias the same heap data, double-free at scope exit, and
# mutating `original` afterwards could corrupt the box copy. The validator
# also bailed on projected (Deref) dsts, so it was UNCAUGHT.
#
# With the fix, the borrowed RHS is cloned at the deref-store boundary, so
# the box copy is INDEPENDENT of the source. Mutating `original` after the
# store leaves the box copy untouched.
#
# Expected (CORRECT) behavior:
#   hello
#   hello world
from std.collections import Box

void main():
    String original = "hello"
    Box[String] b = Box.new("placeholder")
    *b = original                    # borrowed source into owned pointee — must CLONE
    original = original + " world"   # mutate the source after the store
    print(*b)                        # box copy is independent: hello
    print(original)                  # source mutated: hello world
